WEBVTT

00:07.000 --> 00:09.000
[tense, dramatic music playing]

00:15.041 --> 00:16.041
[Momo squawking]

00:18.208 --> 00:20.332
[Aang] Save yourself, Momo!

00:20.333 --> 00:22.333
- [grunting]
- [Momo grunting]

00:24.333 --> 00:25.208
[Aang grunts]

00:25.833 --> 00:26.666
[grunts]

00:27.375 --> 00:28.708
Please don't find me. Please--

00:32.791 --> 00:33.916
[music fades]

00:34.708 --> 00:36.415
Well, it was a good try.

00:36.416 --> 00:37.999
- Really?
- No!

00:38.000 --> 00:40.290
I've seen two-year-olds
hold their ground better.

00:40.291 --> 00:42.290
You're about as stalwart
as a possum chicken.

00:42.291 --> 00:44.165
You know, even Sokka
could've earthbent by now.

00:44.166 --> 00:46.457
Whoa! Take it easy on the poor guy.

00:46.458 --> 00:50.957
Okay, I'll take it easy on him
after he gives me 50 hop squats.

00:50.958 --> 00:52.624
- Yes, Sifu.
- [Sokka scoffs]

00:52.625 --> 00:54.290
- Oh.
- [Aang] One, two…

00:54.291 --> 00:56.707
You know, Aang is a good learner.

00:56.708 --> 00:59.207
And I think
a little positive reinforcement

00:59.208 --> 01:00.290
would go a long way.

01:00.291 --> 01:02.040
Wow, that's actually really helpful.

01:02.041 --> 01:05.040
I'll try and remember that
if he ever does anything positive.

01:05.041 --> 01:07.083
[indistinct chatter]

01:07.583 --> 01:09.999
The sooner we get to Ba Sing Se,
the better.

01:10.000 --> 01:11.125
- Excuse me.
- Oh. Yeah.

01:13.500 --> 01:14.541
[exhales]

01:15.833 --> 01:18.624
- Are you and Suki okay?
- Yeah. We're…

01:18.625 --> 01:21.999
What are you talking about? We're talking.
I said hi to her this morning, so…

01:22.000 --> 01:24.208
We're fine, so just leave me alone.

01:24.916 --> 01:26.665
Come on, Aang. You don't have to keep--

01:26.666 --> 01:27.790
Everybody stop!

01:27.791 --> 01:29.791
[ominous music playing]

01:30.375 --> 01:33.333
There's something… following us.

01:34.208 --> 01:36.208
It's big, and it's moving fast.

01:37.583 --> 01:40.082
- You think it's Azula and her friends?
- Or Zuko again.

01:40.083 --> 01:43.250
- Whatever it is, it's after us.
- No, it's after me.

01:43.916 --> 01:46.207
Everyone should keep moving forward
towards Ba Sing Se.

01:46.208 --> 01:49.290
Good idea! Aang and I will stay behind
and cover everyone's tracks.

01:49.291 --> 01:51.082
- Lead them the wrong way.
- Want me to help?

01:51.083 --> 01:53.499
Oh, don't worry your pretty head
about it, sweetness.

01:53.500 --> 01:55.207
Aang and I have got this.

01:55.208 --> 01:58.125
Come on, baldy. You can
finish your hop squats before the battle.

01:59.083 --> 02:00.957
Why is earthbending so hard for me?

02:00.958 --> 02:02.000
[rumbling]

02:03.541 --> 02:05.833
- [Momo squawking]
- [Appa grunts]

02:07.500 --> 02:08.582
[Momo squawks]

02:08.583 --> 02:12.541
[dramatic music playing]

02:26.791 --> 02:28.708
[music fades]

02:31.250 --> 02:33.708
[Iroh] Earth is the element of strength.

02:35.041 --> 02:38.750
The people of the Earth Kingdom
are resilient and enduring,

02:39.625 --> 02:41.083
like the hills around us.

02:41.583 --> 02:44.375
They face their adversity head-on.

02:44.875 --> 02:47.832
The opposite of earth is air.

02:47.833 --> 02:50.124
Air is the element of freedom.

02:50.125 --> 02:54.624
Like the wind, the Air Nomads live freely
of worldly possessions

02:54.625 --> 02:57.790
and find peace
through detachment and lightness.

02:57.791 --> 03:00.083
The ferry to Ba Sing Se is almost back.
We should head down.

03:01.666 --> 03:04.416
- [indistinct chatter]
- [ferry bell tolling]

03:05.333 --> 03:06.541
We still have time.

03:07.125 --> 03:09.915
The element closest to air is water.

03:09.916 --> 03:13.124
Water is the element of change.

03:13.125 --> 03:17.040
Just as ice transforms to liquid,
then into mist,

03:17.041 --> 03:21.458
the people of the Water Tribes
transform adversity into growth.

03:21.958 --> 03:24.333
Fire is the element of power.

03:29.125 --> 03:33.125
If you want to bring Azula down,
you need to listen to me.

03:33.833 --> 03:35.708
I'm trying to teach you to fight her.

03:36.791 --> 03:38.540
Wait, is this about lightning?

03:38.541 --> 03:42.791
Yes. I'm going to teach you a technique
I designed myself.

03:44.708 --> 03:45.625
Okay.

04:00.166 --> 04:05.583
The key is you must allow the energy
to flow from the tips of your fingers

04:06.083 --> 04:07.458
to your shoulder,

04:08.375 --> 04:10.290
down into your stomach.

04:10.291 --> 04:14.583
The stomach is a bowl
that holds the energy of your body.

04:15.083 --> 04:16.208
From the stomach,

04:16.708 --> 04:21.000
you redirect the energy
up and out through your other arm.

04:23.375 --> 04:24.250
Okay.

04:25.000 --> 04:26.582
[Iroh exhales]

04:26.583 --> 04:28.583
[pensive music playing]

04:34.291 --> 04:35.916
[exhales]

04:40.208 --> 04:43.125
[exhales]

04:46.833 --> 04:48.957
[exhales]

04:48.958 --> 04:51.166
The path through the stomach is critical.

04:54.375 --> 04:57.000
If the lightning detours
through your heart,

04:57.833 --> 04:59.250
it will kill you.

05:00.333 --> 05:01.250
Okay.

05:03.041 --> 05:04.916
[sighs]

05:07.541 --> 05:10.500
[exhales]

05:12.291 --> 05:14.291
[exhales]

05:15.125 --> 05:16.541
[exhales]

05:17.416 --> 05:19.416
[dramatic music playing]

05:20.375 --> 05:22.375
[ferry bell tolling]

05:47.166 --> 05:49.166
[music fades]

05:50.708 --> 05:51.541
[Zuko] Okay.

05:52.041 --> 05:54.665
I got it.
Now… now how do I create the lightning?

05:54.666 --> 05:58.915
No! This is a technique I created
by watching Waterbenders.

05:58.916 --> 06:00.540
It is to redirect lightning.

06:00.541 --> 06:02.790
- Redirect?
- Yes, to defend yourself.

06:02.791 --> 06:06.499
I don't need self-defense.
I need to defeat Azula.

06:06.500 --> 06:08.582
I thought you were teaching me
to bend lightning so--

06:08.583 --> 06:12.957
Lightning is the purest, most dangerous
expression of firebending.

06:12.958 --> 06:17.332
It would be too dangerous for you
until you resolve the turmoil inside.

06:17.333 --> 06:18.290
What turmoil?

06:18.291 --> 06:19.457
[Iroh] Aah!

06:19.458 --> 06:22.207
I'm… I'm sorry. Uncle, I'm… I'm sorry.

06:22.208 --> 06:23.041
I'm okay.

06:24.000 --> 06:25.083
[indistinct chatter]

06:28.583 --> 06:30.583
[suspenseful music playing]

06:32.916 --> 06:33.916
We have to go.

06:39.333 --> 06:40.874
[music fades]

06:40.875 --> 06:43.332
Covering everyone else's tracks worked.

06:43.333 --> 06:45.915
Whatever was following us
is coming this way.

06:45.916 --> 06:48.332
[Aang] If we need to run,
I'll be able to use my glider.

06:48.333 --> 06:50.832
I'm sorry. Why would we run?

06:50.833 --> 06:53.874
In case… we're losing?

06:53.875 --> 06:57.040
[scoffs] This is exactly your problem.

06:57.041 --> 06:59.790
I don't run away from things,
and neither should you.

06:59.791 --> 07:01.999
Azula can bend lightning.

07:02.000 --> 07:06.207
Her fire is blue, and it took seven of us
to make her feel like she was outnumbered.

07:06.208 --> 07:08.790
The second I showed up, she fled.

07:08.791 --> 07:10.375
She barely got away.

07:10.875 --> 07:13.875
So no, I'm not going to run.

07:15.083 --> 07:16.708
[rumbling]

07:18.500 --> 07:21.249
Oh, come on. You've got to be kidding me.

07:21.250 --> 07:22.915
- Well, what is it?
- [Toph] You know what?

07:22.916 --> 07:25.582
- This is gonna be good training for you.
- Training?

07:25.583 --> 07:28.040
You're going to handle this, flighty boy.

07:28.041 --> 07:30.500
And you're gonna do it with earthbending.

07:31.333 --> 07:33.790
Toph, this is not the time
to be messing around.

07:33.791 --> 07:35.290
No, don't worry.

07:35.291 --> 07:37.541
Not even you could lose
to these chuckleheads.

07:38.041 --> 07:40.041
[rumbling continues]

07:42.250 --> 07:43.916
[suspenseful music swells]

07:49.250 --> 07:50.375
[Boulder] Submit!

07:50.875 --> 07:52.457
- [grunts]
- [Aang groans]

07:52.458 --> 07:56.457
We are here to collect you
from the clutches of the Avatar.

07:56.458 --> 08:01.540
At long last, The Boulder has finally
found you, little Beifong.

08:01.541 --> 08:03.790
Oh, help me, O powerful Avatar.

08:03.791 --> 08:05.332
Are you serious right now?

08:05.333 --> 08:07.874
He's going to throw
a bunch of stuff at you.

08:07.875 --> 08:11.708
- Remember… hold your ground.
- Okay.

08:12.208 --> 08:14.457
- Ha!
- Step aside, bald one.

08:14.458 --> 08:15.458
Uh…

08:16.125 --> 08:17.207
No?

08:17.208 --> 08:20.957
- Then prepare to eat… Boulder.
- Ew.

08:20.958 --> 08:24.791
You'll never know how satisfying it was
for The Boulder to learn that…

08:25.291 --> 08:27.083
[grunts] …the Blind Bandit

08:28.541 --> 08:32.874
was a spoiled Beifong princess! Ah!

08:32.875 --> 08:33.708
[Aang yelps]

08:36.416 --> 08:40.458
Plant your feet, wide stance,
and hold your ground.

08:42.333 --> 08:43.832
The Boulder agrees.

08:43.833 --> 08:45.040
Stop running!

08:45.041 --> 08:46.082
And get smashed?

08:46.083 --> 08:48.665
The Boulder has been smashed many times
in the head.

08:48.666 --> 08:50.208
Oh, well, that explains it.

08:56.166 --> 08:59.457
Dig in your heels. Massage the granules.

08:59.458 --> 09:02.374
Mr. Boulder, please refrain
from instructing the Avatar.

09:02.375 --> 09:03.583
[Boulder grunts]

09:04.750 --> 09:06.041
[grunts]

09:07.125 --> 09:11.291
Be one with the stone,
as it cracks your skull!

09:12.708 --> 09:14.374
- Should I be one with it?
- [Toph] No!

09:14.375 --> 09:15.999
[Aang grunts]

09:16.000 --> 09:18.665
- Stop it! You're confusing him!
- I'm not confused.

09:18.666 --> 09:20.540
I just… I can't do it.

09:20.541 --> 09:22.957
Probably because Miss Beifong
never learned the fundamentals.

09:22.958 --> 09:25.125
She's as stubborn as the earth itself.

09:25.625 --> 09:27.374
Hold your ground!

09:27.375 --> 09:29.832
Caress the earth like a lover.

09:29.833 --> 09:31.999
- What?
- Recognize the element to command it.

09:32.000 --> 09:34.707
- Study the terrain.
- [Toph] Stop moving! Quit moving!

09:34.708 --> 09:37.124
- Don't airbend!
- [Xin Fu] Make the elements serve you.

09:37.125 --> 09:39.375
[Toph] Hey! You're making me look bad!

09:40.166 --> 09:41.750
Hey, don't listen to them!

09:46.458 --> 09:48.916
Bravo. You didn't learn a thing.

09:49.708 --> 09:51.915
[Xin Fu] Your mother
is not going to like this!

09:51.916 --> 09:53.415
[Boulder groans]

09:53.416 --> 09:54.874
Not one bit!

09:54.875 --> 09:57.290
[Boulder groans]

09:57.291 --> 09:59.291
[crowd clamoring]

10:06.291 --> 10:09.583
[soldier] The ferry's not ready.
Everyone back up!

10:11.416 --> 10:13.333
[foreboding music playing]

10:14.500 --> 10:15.375
I'm not going.

10:16.708 --> 10:18.540
- What?
- Go without me.

10:18.541 --> 10:20.540
I'm never going back to Ba Sing Se.

10:20.541 --> 10:22.207
[soldier 2] They're coming!

10:22.208 --> 10:24.415
Soldiers, to your defenses!

10:24.416 --> 10:26.499
I'm sorry there wasn't time
to teach you everything.

10:26.500 --> 10:28.875
It's the only place
we can be safe from her.

10:29.375 --> 10:30.832
[woman] Fire Nation!

10:30.833 --> 10:32.874
- [all clamoring]
- [Iroh groans]

10:32.875 --> 10:34.041
[Zuko] Uncle! Uncle!

10:38.041 --> 10:39.041
[groans]

10:39.625 --> 10:40.541
Let's go.

10:44.500 --> 10:45.832
[soldier 3] Launch the ferry!

10:45.833 --> 10:47.250
[soldier 4] We must have order!

10:47.750 --> 10:49.750
[bell ringing]

10:57.166 --> 10:58.125
[Zuko grunts]

11:00.375 --> 11:02.958
Launch the ferry! Launch the ferry!

11:03.458 --> 11:05.500
[tense music playing]

11:16.666 --> 11:19.166
You're okay. You're okay. We made it.

11:19.875 --> 11:22.208
Longshot! There you are.

11:23.791 --> 11:26.874
What are you doing?
You could have gotten left behind!

11:26.875 --> 11:28.624
Look at him, Jet.

11:28.625 --> 11:29.916
He needed help.

11:31.375 --> 11:32.541
[breathing heavily]

11:34.333 --> 11:35.375
Thank you.

11:36.666 --> 11:38.082
[explosion]

11:38.083 --> 11:40.083
[somber music playing]

11:41.291 --> 11:43.166
[people whimpering]

11:53.916 --> 11:55.791
[clamoring]

11:56.291 --> 11:58.374
[thunder rumbles]

11:58.375 --> 12:00.375
[tense music playing]

12:17.708 --> 12:18.958
[music fades]

12:28.625 --> 12:30.375
[Aang] This is the Outer Wall of the city.

12:31.666 --> 12:33.000
But where is everyone?

12:33.500 --> 12:35.666
Oh, I'm sorry. Are we talking again?

12:36.166 --> 12:37.416
Not by choice.

12:40.708 --> 12:43.791
Maybe they already got inside.
Do you see a gate?

12:44.375 --> 12:46.791
[Aang] No. But I see Appa's tracks.

12:49.125 --> 12:50.041
Wait a minute.

12:50.958 --> 12:52.249
Do you hear that?

12:52.250 --> 12:54.124
[Katara] You can't keep us in here!

12:54.125 --> 12:55.832
We came here for help!

12:55.833 --> 12:57.707
Hey, it's your friend, Katara.

12:57.708 --> 12:58.874
[Katara] Let us out!

12:58.875 --> 13:00.000
[pounding on wall]

13:01.166 --> 13:02.207
Katara!

13:02.208 --> 13:03.665
Aang, is that you?

13:03.666 --> 13:05.540
[Aang] Yeah, it's me and Toph.

13:05.541 --> 13:06.540
What happened?

13:06.541 --> 13:09.207
[Katara] The soldiers said
we can't enter the city here.

13:09.208 --> 13:10.207
What soldiers?

13:10.208 --> 13:13.957
We told them we were from Omashu,
and more soldiers came.

13:13.958 --> 13:17.082
They shoved us against the wall,
and now we're all locked up.

13:17.083 --> 13:18.665
Wait a minute, she's right.

13:18.666 --> 13:22.415
I can feel them all down the wall.
Everyone's in their own cell.

13:22.416 --> 13:24.250
[pounding on wall]

13:25.666 --> 13:26.749
What about Appa?

13:26.750 --> 13:28.749
They covered him and Momo in stone.

13:28.750 --> 13:29.666
Open them up.

13:30.875 --> 13:32.957
- Open them all up now!
- All right!

13:32.958 --> 13:34.000
No problem.

13:34.708 --> 13:36.708
[rumbling]

13:37.666 --> 13:40.250
Someone's… fighting me.

13:41.541 --> 13:44.208
Hands up, Earthbender! Against the wall!

13:44.791 --> 13:46.415
Aang, Toph, don't fight them!

13:46.416 --> 13:47.916
[Toph] Get off! Get off of me!

13:49.208 --> 13:50.999
- Toph?
- [rumbling]

13:51.000 --> 13:52.290
Aang!

13:52.291 --> 13:54.082
[rumbling]

13:54.083 --> 13:57.707
Why are you doing this?
Let us out! [yells]

13:57.708 --> 13:59.708
[mysterious music playing]

14:02.375 --> 14:04.375
[coughing]

14:10.958 --> 14:12.958
[indistinct chatter]

14:32.625 --> 14:34.833
I didn't ask you to come after me.

14:36.291 --> 14:37.541
You did that.

14:40.083 --> 14:41.666
It was my fight.

14:43.791 --> 14:45.208
I didn't ask you to.

14:48.833 --> 14:50.250
You follow me.

14:52.458 --> 14:54.291
And then you're gonna abandon me?

14:57.083 --> 14:59.416
You don't get to abandon me.

15:03.041 --> 15:05.291
You don't get that choice.

15:10.875 --> 15:12.416
I'm not gonna let you.

15:22.666 --> 15:24.666
[footsteps approaching]

15:25.458 --> 15:26.915
[Iroh coughs]

15:26.916 --> 15:28.541
[Jet] He's not looking so good.

15:30.541 --> 15:31.625
Sorry, man.

15:35.250 --> 15:36.666
Sorry about before too.

15:38.875 --> 15:40.915
I can see you guys have been through it.

15:40.916 --> 15:42.125
Just like us.

15:46.458 --> 15:48.540
[Iroh coughs]

15:48.541 --> 15:51.540
People are saying we're supposed to
get housing assignments

15:51.541 --> 15:52.750
when we get to the city.

15:54.333 --> 15:58.250
Like they're gonna give us houses when
they won't even give us food on this boat?

16:00.000 --> 16:01.375
I guess we'll see.

16:10.250 --> 16:11.750
[Iroh coughs]

16:13.000 --> 16:14.750
You know where they do have some food?

16:15.333 --> 16:17.083
Captain's quarters.

16:19.333 --> 16:21.125
I saw them taking it up there.

16:22.000 --> 16:26.958
We're talking about a plan
to liberate some meals for ourselves.

16:30.000 --> 16:31.290
You want in?

16:31.291 --> 16:32.833
[somber music playing]

16:34.416 --> 16:35.541
No.

16:37.458 --> 16:39.249
We're just gonna keep our heads down.

16:39.250 --> 16:40.374
[water dripping]

16:40.375 --> 16:41.500
[Iroh coughing]

16:48.125 --> 16:49.791
I bet there's medicine up there too.

16:52.666 --> 16:53.875
[music fades]

16:57.083 --> 16:58.332
[rocks crash]

16:58.333 --> 16:59.874
[soldier] Name and nation of origin.

16:59.875 --> 17:02.583
Katara of the Southern Water Tribe.
I'm traveling with the--

17:06.166 --> 17:10.290
Why would you lock us up?
We're refugees. We came here for help.

17:10.291 --> 17:13.415
You're lucky you're not going to holding
with the rest of them.

17:13.416 --> 17:15.166
But you have an influential friend.

17:15.833 --> 17:17.374
- Katara.
- Aang.

17:17.375 --> 17:19.250
- [Sokka] Oh, you're okay.
- [Katara] Hey.

17:19.750 --> 17:21.791
I thought they were gonna
keep us in there forever.

17:22.291 --> 17:25.375
Me too, but… Toph got us out.

17:25.875 --> 17:28.082
I showed them my family's seal.

17:28.083 --> 17:31.957
Told them that the Beifongs and the Avatar
have important business in the city.

17:31.958 --> 17:35.666
But they'll only let the four of us in.
The Avatar's personal retinue.

17:36.166 --> 17:38.457
We can't leave everyone else
in holding cells.

17:38.458 --> 17:40.415
[scoffs] Hold on.

17:40.416 --> 17:44.540
It took all the clout of my family name
just to do… this.

17:44.541 --> 17:47.874
We'll go see the Earth King
and ask him to help the others.

17:47.875 --> 17:50.582
Your liaison will take you
into the city now.

17:50.583 --> 17:51.957
[woman] Welcome.

17:51.958 --> 17:53.416
I am Joo Dee.

17:53.916 --> 17:56.790
I will be your guide and assistant
in Ba Sing Se.

17:56.791 --> 17:59.166
I hope you weren't too inconvenienced
on your way in.

17:59.750 --> 18:01.208
It wasn't great.

18:02.000 --> 18:02.915
[chuckles]

18:02.916 --> 18:04.750
Thank you, Joo Dee.

18:05.250 --> 18:07.332
We need to see the Earth King right away.

18:07.333 --> 18:10.415
Oh, I can certainly file a request
for an audience.

18:10.416 --> 18:12.790
Oh, no. You don't understand.

18:12.791 --> 18:15.582
We have important information
about the Fire Nation and the war.

18:15.583 --> 18:19.375
I'm sorry, Avatar. You may be confused.

18:19.875 --> 18:22.415
There is no war in Ba Sing Se.

18:22.416 --> 18:24.290
[ominous musical sting plays]

18:24.291 --> 18:25.832
[animals bleating]

18:25.833 --> 18:27.040
[tense music playing]

18:27.041 --> 18:28.790
[Joo Dee] And that's why
the Agrarian Zone,

18:28.791 --> 18:30.790
with its rivers, forest, and farmland,

18:30.791 --> 18:34.916
has kept Ba Sing Se self-sustaining
for generations.

18:36.208 --> 18:38.290
Up ahead is the Inner Wall.

18:38.291 --> 18:40.540
Soon we'll be entering the city proper.

18:40.541 --> 18:42.374
How long will it take
to see the Earth King?

18:42.375 --> 18:44.708
I'll inquire as soon as we disembark.

18:46.166 --> 18:47.541
Here is the city now.

18:48.333 --> 18:50.333
[uplifting mysterious music playing]

19:03.791 --> 19:06.708
[Joo Dee] This is the eclectic Lower Ring.

19:08.041 --> 19:12.250
Home to our hardworking tradespeople
and artisans.

19:12.791 --> 19:17.374
Joo Dee, my sky bison
could just fly alongside us.

19:17.375 --> 19:19.790
Then your Earthbenders
wouldn't need to push him.

19:19.791 --> 19:20.832
Oh.

19:20.833 --> 19:24.249
I'm afraid the citizens of Ba Sing Se
would find that distressing.

19:24.250 --> 19:26.833
This city is a no-fly zone.

19:27.416 --> 19:29.582
If you look ahead,
you can see the Middle Ring,

19:29.583 --> 19:32.915
containing our best shops,
restaurants, and schools.

19:32.916 --> 19:34.250
Oh, shops?

19:34.750 --> 19:36.290
We don't have time for shopping.

19:36.291 --> 19:38.874
Would it be possible
to take us directly to the Earth King?

19:38.875 --> 19:42.374
It'd be impolite if I did not escort you
to your lodgings first.

19:42.375 --> 19:46.624
I am thrilled to tell you the Avatar villa
is situated in the Upper Ring.

19:46.625 --> 19:49.665
That's where our royalty
and nobility reside.

19:49.666 --> 19:52.957
It is an elegant neighborhood
with gardens and spas.

19:52.958 --> 19:55.749
We're right next to the Earth King. Great!

19:55.750 --> 19:57.457
- Maybe we could--
- Actually!

19:57.458 --> 20:01.915
Friends, I think we all would enjoy
a little respite.

20:01.916 --> 20:04.790
Ba Sing Se is famous for its hospitality.

20:04.791 --> 20:09.874
We consider it a privilege
to be hosting the Avatar, Toph Beifong,

20:09.875 --> 20:12.540
and esteemed members
of the Southern Water Tribe.

20:12.541 --> 20:14.083
I'll be back with refreshments.

20:14.958 --> 20:17.124
Everyone, pipe down!

20:17.125 --> 20:19.958
Can't you dummies tell?
We're being handled.

20:20.541 --> 20:22.666
- What does that mean?
- [sighs] Okay.

20:23.333 --> 20:25.582
A city is like a giant machine.

20:25.583 --> 20:28.915
But instead of steam or coal,
it runs on bureaucracy.

20:28.916 --> 20:31.582
Yeah, we have bureaucracy
in the Southern Water Tribe too.

20:31.583 --> 20:34.375
All requests have to go through me…
and then Gran Gran.

20:35.041 --> 20:37.290
Yes, bureaucracy is people.

20:37.291 --> 20:41.249
But here,
bureaucracy is a bunch of useless people

20:41.250 --> 20:43.540
standing between you and what you want.

20:43.541 --> 20:45.665
They handle your requests.

20:45.666 --> 20:47.749
And you have to make them feel important.

20:47.750 --> 20:52.749
Otherwise, they just kick you back
to the start of this great, stupid maze.

20:52.750 --> 20:55.415
That's why we have to be nice to Joo Dee.

20:55.416 --> 20:58.207
Otherwise, we lose
our only connection to the king.

20:58.208 --> 21:00.124
Just trust me, okay?

21:00.125 --> 21:01.374
I know cities.

21:01.375 --> 21:05.749
You may know cities, but you're new
to how this Avatar thing works.

21:05.750 --> 21:07.540
- Aang is important.
- [Toph] Uh-huh.

21:07.541 --> 21:10.749
He's so important
that I had to rescue him from prison!

21:10.750 --> 21:12.750
[peaceful music playing]

21:13.666 --> 21:16.999
[Joo Dee] We hope
you'll find the villa satisfactory.

21:17.000 --> 21:20.666
It is where we've hosted
many Avatars of the past.

21:21.291 --> 21:25.749
All meals will be delivered promptly
by your personal caterer.

21:25.750 --> 21:28.957
And beyond that are your private suites.

21:28.958 --> 21:32.541
Your sky bison will stay
in the adjoining barn.

21:33.041 --> 21:34.499
[knocking on door]

21:34.500 --> 21:35.333
[man] Excuse me.

21:35.833 --> 21:36.749
Hello.

21:36.750 --> 21:37.750
[Joo Dee gasps]

21:38.833 --> 21:40.333
[man] I'm so glad I caught you.

21:40.833 --> 21:42.208
I am Long Feng.

21:42.708 --> 21:43.958
Cultural Minister.

21:45.666 --> 21:47.332
This is Minister Long Feng.

21:47.333 --> 21:51.165
He's the senior official
who oversees cultural life in the city.

21:51.166 --> 21:52.165
I have news for you.

21:52.166 --> 21:55.875
But first, before that,
if you would indulge me,

21:57.541 --> 22:00.458
I brought some… welcome gifts.

22:02.750 --> 22:04.624
- Here.
- Huh. Thanks.

22:04.625 --> 22:05.791
[Long Feng] And, uh…

22:06.333 --> 22:07.332
[gasps]

22:07.333 --> 22:09.040
Candied sea prunes?

22:09.041 --> 22:11.040
- Miss Beifong.
- [Katara] Just like home.

22:11.041 --> 22:12.166
[Sokka gasps]

22:13.750 --> 22:14.665
[Katara sighs]

22:14.666 --> 22:15.875
- [uncorks bottle]
- [Toph sniffs]

22:17.083 --> 22:20.165
Is this… mineral salt to soak my feet?

22:20.166 --> 22:22.541
Earthbending can get tiring.

22:26.250 --> 22:28.416
A stone from the top
of the Eastern Air Temple.

22:30.291 --> 22:32.666
The ancestral home of the sky bison.

22:33.250 --> 22:36.041
And also the birthplace of airbending.

22:36.625 --> 22:38.790
I hope, uh, this is appropriate.

22:38.791 --> 22:42.583
What do you give an Air Nomad
who is in want of nothing?

22:43.291 --> 22:44.750
That's where I met Appa.

22:45.250 --> 22:46.791
I'll keep this with me always.

22:48.458 --> 22:50.207
And now for the news.

22:50.208 --> 22:54.290
The king has granted asylum
to all Omashan refugees.

22:54.291 --> 22:57.249
We are in the process of settling them
in the Lower Ring

22:57.250 --> 23:01.416
and providing them with food vouchers,
necessities, and stipends

23:02.000 --> 23:03.374
until they find work.

23:03.375 --> 23:08.041
All I ask is, uh…
if you can confirm this roster.

23:08.541 --> 23:11.083
- Don't want to miss anyone.
- Yes, of course.

23:12.416 --> 23:13.707
Yeah, everyone's accounted for.

23:13.708 --> 23:16.833
Yeah, Suki and the other Kyoshi Warriors
are listed…

23:17.458 --> 23:18.624
Could we see them?

23:18.625 --> 23:20.875
- Uh, see… see everyone?
- [Long Feng] Of course.

23:21.875 --> 23:24.625
Could you arrange a carriage, please,
Joo Dee?

23:27.125 --> 23:29.833
I've also heard
you wish to speak to King Kuei.

23:30.416 --> 23:34.415
As it happens, the king is having a party
at the Royal Palace tonight,

23:34.416 --> 23:37.375
and he would like for you
to be his honored guests.

23:37.875 --> 23:39.665
We would like that very much.

23:39.666 --> 23:40.958
It's settled, then.

23:41.833 --> 23:45.125
You visit your friends,
some rest, and a party.

23:46.000 --> 23:47.125
I must say

23:48.416 --> 23:51.250
it is the honor of a lifetime

23:51.791 --> 23:55.125
to be helping
the Avatar and his companions.

23:57.333 --> 24:00.665
Honor of a lifetime to help the Avatar.

24:00.666 --> 24:01.749
See, Toph?

24:01.750 --> 24:03.165
No, I don't.

24:03.166 --> 24:05.499
Oh. No, no I'm… I didn't mean it--

24:05.500 --> 24:08.040
Yeah, yeah, as fun as it is
to listen to you squirm,

24:08.041 --> 24:09.707
you're still wrong.

24:09.708 --> 24:12.375
This will not be
as easy as he makes it sound.

24:13.041 --> 24:15.250
Whatever. Ignore me at your peril.

24:16.166 --> 24:17.290
[huffs]

24:17.291 --> 24:18.915
Great. I wanna call this room.

24:18.916 --> 24:21.040
- I'm gonna go in here. Yeah.
- [Katara] What? No, what?

24:21.041 --> 24:21.957
I wanted this one.

24:21.958 --> 24:24.165
- [Sokka] I really like it.
- [Katara] I like it too.

24:24.166 --> 24:26.332
[peaceful music playing]

24:26.333 --> 24:27.250
[sighs]

24:28.750 --> 24:30.750
[indistinct chatter]

24:31.541 --> 24:33.125
[Sokka] So where'd Teo go?

24:33.708 --> 24:35.874
He wanted to be more helpful
with the war effort,

24:35.875 --> 24:38.124
so he left to find
some resistance fighters

24:38.125 --> 24:40.457
that Kyoshi Warriors
told him about in the North.

24:40.458 --> 24:41.666
He brought my designs

24:42.375 --> 24:45.708
so he could build more gliders
and teach others how to

24:46.708 --> 24:49.125
fight the Fire Nation from the air.

24:53.625 --> 24:54.958
I'm so proud of him.

24:58.625 --> 25:02.416
They said there would be
no flying over the city, and

25:04.083 --> 25:05.166
Teo's a flyer.

25:08.083 --> 25:09.250
I'm sorry.

25:14.541 --> 25:15.458
Sokka,

25:16.291 --> 25:18.375
the Kyoshi Warriors
have left the city too.

25:19.083 --> 25:20.291
Suki said

25:21.166 --> 25:25.125
there was no need for warriors
in a city with no war.

25:26.000 --> 25:28.000
[somber music playing]

25:30.750 --> 25:31.583
Uh…

25:32.166 --> 25:33.583
Did she say anything else?

25:35.875 --> 25:37.458
No, she didn't.

25:41.291 --> 25:42.290
Um… uh,

25:42.291 --> 25:45.874
well, you're busy here,
so… uh, I'll leave you to it.

25:45.875 --> 25:48.665
Sokka. Sokka, if you wanted
to come back tomorrow to help me,

25:48.666 --> 25:50.416
I could use your thoughts and…

25:52.625 --> 25:55.416
if you wanted to come back tomorrow
just to talk, I'm here for that too.

25:58.916 --> 25:59.791
Thanks.

26:10.000 --> 26:11.416
You know, yesterday,

26:12.208 --> 26:14.291
I didn't know if we'd see another sunrise.

26:15.208 --> 26:19.250
And now I'm thinking about
opening a flower shop again.

26:20.416 --> 26:21.250
[chuckles]

26:24.041 --> 26:26.124
[Katara] Praying
to the Painted Lady worked.

26:26.125 --> 26:28.875
Well, prayers only work
when we act on them, right?

26:37.583 --> 26:39.125
Diya, what happened?

26:39.750 --> 26:43.083
A spider bit her
when we were locked in that room.

26:44.166 --> 26:48.666
I made a balm with aloe berries,
but it doesn't look like it's helping.

26:49.916 --> 26:51.541
Well, venom is a liquid.

26:52.250 --> 26:53.833
Maybe I can bend it out.

26:54.583 --> 26:55.666
Can I see your arm?

27:00.666 --> 27:02.666
[mysterious music playing]

27:04.500 --> 27:06.500
[liquid gurgling]

27:07.250 --> 27:08.250
Ow!

27:09.000 --> 27:10.000
I'm sorry.

27:12.333 --> 27:14.124
I guess I can't do it.

27:14.125 --> 27:15.832
It's a shame we don't have golden nettle.

27:15.833 --> 27:19.291
Then I could make a poultice
that would just clear it right up, but

27:20.000 --> 27:21.582
it's really rare.

27:21.583 --> 27:23.416
Thanks for trying, Katara.

27:24.750 --> 27:27.208
Katara, there you are.

27:29.416 --> 27:32.541
You must inform me
if you are going to depart from the group.

27:33.541 --> 27:35.915
I was just saying hi to Amita.

27:35.916 --> 27:39.165
But I was meant to escort you
on your visit to the Lower Ring.

27:39.166 --> 27:41.125
We must keep to the itinerary.

27:41.958 --> 27:44.499
Are you saying I can't just walk around
and talk to people?

27:44.500 --> 27:46.332
Of course that's not what I'm saying.

27:46.333 --> 27:50.874
I only want to ensure that the Avatar
and his companions remain in good standing

27:50.875 --> 27:54.583
while their request to speak with
the Earth King is in process.

27:55.666 --> 27:57.291
Visiting hours are over now.

27:57.791 --> 27:59.665
[Katara] Yeah,
I'm telling you, it was weird.

27:59.666 --> 28:02.832
Like I've been telling you,
you've gotta play along.

28:02.833 --> 28:06.165
It feels wrong talking about the war
dressed so… fancy.

28:06.166 --> 28:09.000
That's gorgeous! I mean, so is mine, but…

28:09.500 --> 28:10.832
What is this, silk?

28:10.833 --> 28:13.499
[scoffs] They even gave us makeup.

28:13.500 --> 28:16.249
When the Kyoshi Warriors put on makeup,
it's to go to battle.

28:16.250 --> 28:18.582
A party is a battle!

28:18.583 --> 28:19.665
[tense music playing]

28:19.666 --> 28:23.875
There is nothing less enjoyable
than a high-society soirée.

28:24.500 --> 28:27.249
Everybody is there
because they want something,

28:27.250 --> 28:29.125
and nobody is there to have fun.

28:30.625 --> 28:32.625
Take the four of us, for example.

28:33.208 --> 28:35.624
We're all going
so we can speak to the king,

28:35.625 --> 28:38.040
which means
we all better make a good impression

28:38.041 --> 28:42.750
and behave like elites
worthy of his divine royal audience.

28:43.500 --> 28:46.083
That means bowing correctly.

28:48.208 --> 28:51.415
Always saying "yes,"
even when you mean "no."

28:51.416 --> 28:56.208
Or even better, just say,
"Huh, perhaps" to everything.

28:56.791 --> 29:00.291
Speak agreeably,
always with a faint smile.

29:01.166 --> 29:04.708
But you do not wanna show teeth.
You never wanna show teeth.

29:06.291 --> 29:07.582
[Sokka] Uh…

29:07.583 --> 29:09.915
No, Sokka. I don't think it's that.

29:09.916 --> 29:11.457
I think I prefer a real battle.

29:11.458 --> 29:13.915
I think I prefer the Kyoshi Warriors.

29:13.916 --> 29:17.040
Perhaps I should have accepted
Suki's offer.

29:17.041 --> 29:18.707
- When did she ask?
- Suki asked you?

29:18.708 --> 29:20.082
- Did she send a hawk--
- You going?

29:20.083 --> 29:23.582
No, it was before we got here,
and I didn't say yes, obviously.

29:23.583 --> 29:29.000
I just… thought it was nice
that she thought I was worthy.

29:31.833 --> 29:32.833
[Sokka sighs]

29:39.375 --> 29:44.916
Well, as long as Toph is here to guide us,
we'll be okay.

29:46.083 --> 29:51.041
- It'll be like parties your parents host.
- Oh, no, Avatar, this will be much worse.

29:51.916 --> 29:53.916
[intense, dramatic music playing]

30:06.416 --> 30:08.833
It's customary
to enter the party in pairs.

30:23.750 --> 30:24.625
Yeah?

30:27.291 --> 30:28.250
You look…

30:30.250 --> 30:31.083
nice.

30:31.833 --> 30:32.750
So do you.

30:34.291 --> 30:35.958
Aang, no teeth.

30:37.625 --> 30:38.500
Right.

30:41.000 --> 30:43.000
[upbeat, festive music playing]

30:45.625 --> 30:47.625
[indistinct chatter]

31:05.500 --> 31:06.500
[crowd exclaims]

31:09.958 --> 31:10.958
[crowd exclaims]

31:11.750 --> 31:16.666
How brave you are
to dress so rustically in the palace.

31:17.375 --> 31:19.582
Well, they actually told us to wear these…

31:19.583 --> 31:21.040
[Sokka] Right, yeah.

31:21.041 --> 31:22.332
May I?

31:22.333 --> 31:23.290
[Katara] Oh…

31:23.291 --> 31:25.290
- [music stops]
- [light applause]

31:25.291 --> 31:28.874
[woman] It's said a visit from the Avatar
brings good fortune.

31:28.875 --> 31:31.457
- I just opened a lakefront estate.
- [Toph chuckles]

31:31.458 --> 31:36.165
Perhaps, madam, if the Avatar
can find room in his schedule.

31:36.166 --> 31:38.457
We came here
to deliver a group of refugees.

31:38.458 --> 31:40.915
Their city was overtaken
by a Fire Nation army.

31:40.916 --> 31:43.249
Fire Nation still has an army?

31:43.250 --> 31:44.415
[man] No!

31:44.416 --> 31:48.790
They stopped fighting after we drove them
from our walls in defeat.

31:48.791 --> 31:52.332
The Fire Nation hasn't stopped fighting
for a hundred years.

31:52.333 --> 31:54.624
All over the Earth Kingdom,
they're waging war.

31:54.625 --> 31:57.041
[woman 2] There is no war in Ba Sing Se.

31:58.500 --> 32:02.290
General Sung, Supreme Commander
of the Forces of the Outer Wall.

32:02.291 --> 32:05.750
So you're the Avatar
who caused us so much trouble.

32:06.500 --> 32:07.707
[Toph] Mmm.

32:07.708 --> 32:09.707
How do you do, General?

32:09.708 --> 32:13.625
We owe all our thanks to your soldiers
for granting us entry into the city.

32:14.208 --> 32:16.457
At least he's in the good company
of a Beifong.

32:16.458 --> 32:20.291
Yes, well, I have been teaching him
the ways of the city.

32:22.541 --> 32:25.874
General, you know
the Fire Nation hasn't stopped fighting.

32:25.875 --> 32:28.457
We have an urgent message
that we need to tell the king.

32:28.458 --> 32:31.582
After the failed siege,
the wall was fortified.

32:31.583 --> 32:35.208
Ba Sing Se will remain impenetrable
for centuries to come.

32:36.333 --> 32:39.790
Out there,
the Fire Nation is growing in power.

32:39.791 --> 32:42.500
What does "out there" have to do with us?

32:44.291 --> 32:45.374
[tense music playing]

32:45.375 --> 32:47.583
It's best if you accelerate his education.

32:56.375 --> 33:01.666
I heard a terrible rumor
that your people eat sea prune?

33:02.958 --> 33:04.374
That's actually true.

33:04.375 --> 33:05.415
[laughs] Oh.

33:05.416 --> 33:09.708
Well, here, our people drink cactus juice.

33:11.333 --> 33:12.166
Okay.

33:12.750 --> 33:14.458
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

33:14.958 --> 33:18.082
It's harvested from cacti
native to the Si Wong Desert

33:18.083 --> 33:21.375
that secretes the juice
as a defense mechanism against predators.

33:21.875 --> 33:23.874
It interferes with brain activity.

33:23.875 --> 33:26.540
Sometimes… permanently.

33:26.541 --> 33:29.000
Ah, this guy is such a bore.

33:30.958 --> 33:34.915
I'm Zei, Professor of Anthropology
at Ba Sing Se University.

33:34.916 --> 33:36.083
I'm Sokka.

33:36.958 --> 33:37.791
Uh…

33:38.291 --> 33:40.499
Oh, I believe
this is the traditional greeting

33:40.500 --> 33:42.500
for men of the Southern Water Tribe.

33:43.541 --> 33:44.583
Is that okay?

33:45.250 --> 33:46.083
Yeah, it's great!

33:55.666 --> 33:57.333
[mysterious music playing]

34:09.875 --> 34:12.000
[whispering] Those are
the crates with the food.

34:45.875 --> 34:47.374
What's taking so long?

34:47.375 --> 34:49.374
Jet, there's a lot more food here.

34:49.375 --> 34:50.291
[Jet] So?

34:50.791 --> 34:53.333
- We could feed the others.
- What others?

35:14.875 --> 35:16.999
[indistinct voices approaching]

35:17.000 --> 35:18.916
We gotta go. Someone's coming.

35:29.208 --> 35:31.583
[panting]

35:32.875 --> 35:33.875
[indistinct voices]

35:41.291 --> 35:42.458
Thanks.

35:51.291 --> 35:55.125
[uplifting, mystical music playing]

36:00.708 --> 36:02.374
[woman] Yoo-hoo! Toph Beifong!

36:02.375 --> 36:03.499
[chuckles]

36:03.500 --> 36:06.290
So glad you could come to Ba Sing Se.

36:06.291 --> 36:09.374
I'm sorry.
I don't believe we've met, Lady--

36:09.375 --> 36:13.541
Lord and Lady Ouyang.
We're friends of your father's.

36:14.416 --> 36:17.290
- Are you here to accept the proposal?
- Proposal?

36:17.291 --> 36:21.166
Our son's marriage proposal that was sent
to your parents' winter manor?

36:22.750 --> 36:23.999
Um… [clears throat]

36:24.000 --> 36:27.999
Perhaps I should send a hawk to my parents
to inquire further.

36:28.000 --> 36:31.499
Have they received
our son's portrait as well?

36:31.500 --> 36:35.332
His name is Pan Hua.
He manages our newest restaurant.

36:35.333 --> 36:36.249
Charming.

36:36.250 --> 36:37.374
Oh, yes.

36:37.375 --> 36:41.332
Isn't he the young man who managed
your former restaurant into the ground?

36:41.333 --> 36:44.707
Doesn't your son take a carriage
to the Middle Ring

36:44.708 --> 36:46.832
to study at a trade college?

36:46.833 --> 36:50.082
At least my son is getting an education,
unlike some people.

36:50.083 --> 36:52.624
Our son's restaurant
is the talk of the palace.

36:52.625 --> 36:57.374
[Sokka] We have, like, a spherical roof
with no internal pillars.

36:57.375 --> 37:02.165
That way, the pressure
is distributed evenly from the top down.

37:02.166 --> 37:04.207
The snow bricks support themselves.

37:04.208 --> 37:06.415
Wow. Domed ice houses.

37:06.416 --> 37:08.583
- Mm-hmm.
- Huh! So ingenious!

37:09.083 --> 37:12.124
See, we… we do everything practically.

37:12.125 --> 37:16.208
And what was the practical purpose
of domesticating the otter penguin?

37:17.250 --> 37:18.333
Uh…

37:19.708 --> 37:20.708
Companionship.

37:21.208 --> 37:23.375
- Ha! Well said.
- Yep.

37:23.875 --> 37:25.790
So you were
in the Northern Water Tribe, right?

37:25.791 --> 37:27.666
Oh, I have so many questions.

37:28.583 --> 37:29.749
Oh, about the North?

37:29.750 --> 37:32.708
Yes, I'm interested in
their spiritual leadership structure.

37:33.500 --> 37:34.415
Right.

37:34.416 --> 37:37.374
Now, I've read that they have
a patriarchal society,

37:37.375 --> 37:39.999
but that spiritual leadership
can be undertaken by women.

37:40.000 --> 37:41.915
And it feels like a little contradiction,

37:41.916 --> 37:47.249
except that the spiritual leader seems
to be chosen by the ocean or moon spirit.

37:47.250 --> 37:49.415
[fading] I suppose
they don't really have a gender…

37:49.416 --> 37:50.582
[Sokka's mind] Please don't.

37:50.583 --> 37:53.249
Please, you don't have to do this. Yue!

37:53.250 --> 37:55.250
[indistinct chatter]

37:59.625 --> 38:00.500
[woman] Golden nettle.

38:01.666 --> 38:03.124
Lovely, no?

38:03.125 --> 38:05.541
The king cultivates them
in his private garden.

38:06.750 --> 38:08.291
Lovely, yes.

38:10.250 --> 38:12.875
They have tons
of medicinal properties too.

38:13.375 --> 38:16.249
People could use them.
People in the Lower Ring.

38:16.250 --> 38:17.208
I like how they smell.

38:29.083 --> 38:30.500
[sinister chord plays]

38:31.125 --> 38:32.083
[gasps]

38:34.000 --> 38:35.790
- [woman 2] Proposals?
- [woman 3] Mm-hmm.

38:35.791 --> 38:37.124
[woman 2] Who'd wanna marry her?

38:37.125 --> 38:39.082
[woman 3] What instrument
could she even play?

38:39.083 --> 38:41.166
- The dinner gong. [laughs]
- [woman 2 laughs]

38:42.833 --> 38:45.540
These people are only after her fortune.

38:45.541 --> 38:47.582
[woman 3] If only the Beifongs had a son.

38:47.583 --> 38:48.624
[chuckles]

38:48.625 --> 38:49.790
Do you think her parents…

38:49.791 --> 38:50.750
Toph.

38:52.375 --> 38:54.166
Leave it, and don't make a scene.

38:54.750 --> 38:55.707
But they're being--

38:55.708 --> 38:58.000
I said don't make a scene, sugar queen.

38:58.583 --> 39:00.749
- [woman 2] How embarrassing.
- [woman 3 laughs]

39:00.750 --> 39:02.957
[woman 2] Her makeup
looks like a baboon's butt.

39:02.958 --> 39:03.791
[both laugh]

39:05.250 --> 39:06.708
[woman 2 screams]

39:07.583 --> 39:08.582
Oh my God!

39:08.583 --> 39:10.707
What happened?

39:10.708 --> 39:12.665
My makeup!

39:12.666 --> 39:13.958
[both] Our makeup!

39:14.833 --> 39:15.750
[chuckles]

39:16.250 --> 39:18.957
Did you just bend their drinks
into their faces?

39:18.958 --> 39:21.750
Well, I'm not gonna let anyone talk
about my friend like that.

39:23.791 --> 39:24.750
Your friend?

39:25.916 --> 39:28.166
Yeah, Toph. You're my friend.

39:28.666 --> 39:32.500
We went through a lot to get here.
How could we not be friends?

39:33.625 --> 39:35.833
I mean,
I've been kind of mean to you. [chuckles]

39:37.250 --> 39:38.708
Mostly, you just tell the truth.

39:41.083 --> 39:43.125
You just don't do it very nicely.

39:46.166 --> 39:47.083
Yeah.

39:47.833 --> 39:49.125
I don't. I'm…

39:49.625 --> 39:50.750
I'm not nice.

39:51.833 --> 39:53.625
That's my problem.

39:54.208 --> 39:55.833
I've been too nice lately!

39:56.583 --> 39:59.457
- Well, that's not quite what I was--
- [Toph] Thank you, Katara.

39:59.458 --> 40:02.499
And hey, if you ever need me
to drop a big ol' rock on someone's head,

40:02.500 --> 40:04.083
just say the word.

40:05.333 --> 40:06.458
Uh…

40:11.291 --> 40:13.333
Toph, everybody's talking to me. I--

40:14.666 --> 40:17.165
I ran away from home,
like, a really comfortable home,

40:17.166 --> 40:18.707
to try and teach you.

40:18.708 --> 40:20.458
- I know.
- [Toph] Be quiet.

40:21.208 --> 40:24.540
I crossed half the Earth Kingdom on foot
just to get here.

40:24.541 --> 40:26.874
- Well…
- To the city, which I hate.

40:26.875 --> 40:30.124
And I had to use my name,
which I never wanted to do again.

40:30.125 --> 40:35.249
And now every conniving sycophant
is socially climbing out of the walls

40:35.250 --> 40:37.666
to try and marry me,
which I don't wanna do.

40:38.250 --> 40:42.333
All to teach the Avatar to earthbend,
and you can't even kick a rock.

40:42.916 --> 40:44.541
- But--
- [Toph] But what?

40:45.416 --> 40:46.375
I'll work harder.

40:47.333 --> 40:49.458
No. You won't.

40:50.375 --> 40:51.915
You wanna know why?

40:51.916 --> 40:53.333
Because I quit.

40:54.000 --> 40:55.624
- You can't quit.
- [Toph] I can quit.

40:55.625 --> 40:57.666
You can't learn.

40:58.375 --> 41:01.540
How am I supposed to learn?
All you do is shout at me.

41:01.541 --> 41:04.415
[laughs] Oh!
Maybe it's 'cause you don't listen!

41:04.416 --> 41:07.165
No wonder it took you years
to learn how to waterbend.

41:07.166 --> 41:09.249
At least I had a good teacher for that.

41:09.250 --> 41:11.750
Oh, okay. So you think this is my fault?

41:12.333 --> 41:14.332
- Maybe.
- Maybe?

41:14.333 --> 41:17.124
Okay, well, maybe you'll never learn this.

41:17.125 --> 41:20.332
Maybe water and air is
all you'll ever bend.

41:20.333 --> 41:23.541
Maybe you're nothing but a half-atar.

41:24.083 --> 41:25.208
Enough!

41:29.083 --> 41:31.083
[triumphant music playing]

41:31.625 --> 41:32.708
You did it.

41:33.500 --> 41:35.791
While we were arguing,
you held your ground.

41:36.666 --> 41:38.082
I did it.

41:38.083 --> 41:40.416
I held my ground, and I earthbent!

41:42.041 --> 41:44.333
I'm the greatest earthbending teacher
in the world!

41:46.041 --> 41:47.582
[Katara] Here you are.

41:47.583 --> 41:49.124
[Sokka breathes shakily]

41:49.125 --> 41:50.083
Here I am.

41:52.500 --> 41:53.790
[Katara] Are you okay?

41:53.791 --> 41:55.790
[somber music playing]

41:55.791 --> 41:57.875
I messed it all up with Suki.

41:59.708 --> 42:00.750
Suki?

42:01.458 --> 42:02.665
No, Suki likes you.

42:02.666 --> 42:04.957
Yeah, she did, and I liked her.

42:04.958 --> 42:06.291
And then I just

42:07.500 --> 42:08.665
pushed her away!

42:08.666 --> 42:11.250
And I didn't even get to apologize
when she was

42:12.166 --> 42:13.250
right there.

42:14.416 --> 42:16.583
She was right there.

42:18.958 --> 42:20.957
I was about to tell her I was sorry.

42:20.958 --> 42:23.791
And before I could open my mouth,
a wall came up between us.

42:24.916 --> 42:27.708
She was here, and then she was gone.

42:29.250 --> 42:31.250
I don't know why I pushed her away.

42:33.458 --> 42:34.583
Sokka,

42:35.375 --> 42:37.291
why do you think you might have?

42:38.333 --> 42:39.375
Because…

42:42.833 --> 42:43.708
Yue.

42:46.541 --> 42:49.999
I didn't wanna lose Suki
the same way I lost Yue,

42:50.000 --> 42:51.541
but I lost her anyway.

42:52.541 --> 42:54.083
Why am I not over this?

42:54.833 --> 42:56.333
What is wrong with me?

43:00.250 --> 43:01.250
Sokka.

43:02.291 --> 43:04.250
That's not how grief works.

43:05.833 --> 43:07.749
So what? I'm just gonna be
screwed up forever,

43:07.750 --> 43:10.832
never knowing if something's
gonna tip me over the edge?

43:10.833 --> 43:12.125
I don't know.

43:18.000 --> 43:19.541
I'm not over Mom.

43:23.500 --> 43:26.750
There will never be a day
that I don't think about Mom.

43:31.333 --> 43:32.666
But I guess…

43:34.666 --> 43:36.375
that's why I've got you.

43:36.958 --> 43:38.250
And you've got me.

43:40.833 --> 43:43.583
Let's just talk about these things
from now on.

43:44.666 --> 43:45.583
Yeah.

43:48.791 --> 43:49.750
I'd like that.

43:53.708 --> 43:54.791
What is that?

43:58.458 --> 44:00.583
Um… it's cactus juice.

44:01.375 --> 44:02.416
[horns playing]

44:07.416 --> 44:09.416
[dramatic music playing]

44:16.541 --> 44:17.625
[Aang gasps]

44:22.000 --> 44:22.999
Now's my chance.

44:23.000 --> 44:24.750
- Wait, don't forget to bow.
- [exhales sharply]

44:29.250 --> 44:30.540
I'm Avatar Aang. I must--

44:30.541 --> 44:31.458
Step back.

44:32.750 --> 44:34.249
I must speak with--

44:34.250 --> 44:36.958
Step… back.

44:38.125 --> 44:39.458
[Long Feng] Avatar Aang,

44:40.750 --> 44:43.791
you… you can't
approach the king like that.

44:46.041 --> 44:47.166
Come.

44:48.875 --> 44:50.958
[Aang] I have a message
that the king needs to hear.

44:53.000 --> 44:55.000
Please, Long Feng. It's important.

44:57.208 --> 44:58.833
I'll ask if he'll see you.

45:00.625 --> 45:01.583
Thank you.

45:02.083 --> 45:02.958
Okay.

45:04.791 --> 45:05.791
[Aang sighs]

45:15.333 --> 45:17.333
[dramatic music playing]

45:51.791 --> 45:53.791
[music fades]

45:55.333 --> 45:56.416
Of course.

45:57.250 --> 45:58.125
Thank you.

46:00.125 --> 46:01.125
[Smellerbee] Here you go.

46:01.875 --> 46:03.083
[woman gasps]

46:03.625 --> 46:05.375
Oh, bless you.

46:12.666 --> 46:13.625
Jet.

46:16.666 --> 46:18.666
[sentimental music playing]

46:35.791 --> 46:38.083
It's okay. It's willow bark tea.

46:45.333 --> 46:46.166
[sips]

46:47.541 --> 46:48.458
[coughs]

46:50.083 --> 46:51.333
It's bracing.

46:54.083 --> 46:55.583
But it'll do the job.

47:00.500 --> 47:01.958
You look different.

47:03.541 --> 47:04.458
Do I?

47:12.708 --> 47:14.666
[Smellerbee] Share these with the others.

47:18.041 --> 47:19.166
Thank you.

47:38.166 --> 47:40.166
[foreboding music playing]

47:44.375 --> 47:45.707
A hundred years ago,

47:45.708 --> 47:48.957
the Fire Nation used the comet's power
to kill the Air Nomads.

47:48.958 --> 47:52.624
So it only makes sense
that they would do the same thing again.

47:52.625 --> 47:54.290
And it's on its way back.

47:54.291 --> 47:56.208
Our friend Sai has proof.

47:57.291 --> 47:59.165
This is grave indeed.

47:59.166 --> 48:02.832
Now you know why I need to tell
the Earth King as soon as possible.

48:02.833 --> 48:04.249
[Long Feng sighs]

48:04.250 --> 48:05.208
[Aang sighs]

48:08.375 --> 48:10.750
There is something

48:12.500 --> 48:14.333
you should know about the king.

48:15.041 --> 48:16.333
He is beloved.

48:16.833 --> 48:19.790
But he can be a difficult man,

48:19.791 --> 48:22.040
rigidly adhering to rituals

48:22.041 --> 48:25.207
and ruling Ba Sing Se
like it was his perfect domain.

48:25.208 --> 48:29.083
He'll close his mind to any news
that goes against his point of view.

48:29.583 --> 48:31.541
Just like the people at the party.

48:32.208 --> 48:35.082
It's like they don't even know
there's a war going on.

48:35.083 --> 48:36.291
Exactly.

48:36.791 --> 48:38.541
And this is because of the king.

48:39.041 --> 48:41.707
He forbids people to speak of war.

48:41.708 --> 48:43.040
And anyone who mentions it

48:43.041 --> 48:46.415
attracts the attention
of the king's guards, the Dai Li.

48:46.416 --> 48:49.541
They are his eyes and ears
everywhere in the city.

48:50.083 --> 48:51.915
There must be a way
to make him see the truth.

48:51.916 --> 48:53.583
I wish there were.

48:54.708 --> 48:56.540
He rules by divine right,

48:56.541 --> 48:59.040
believing that,
as long as the spirits will it,

48:59.041 --> 49:00.583
he is infallible.

49:04.416 --> 49:05.333
But…

49:07.041 --> 49:09.333
but you are a bridge to the spirits.

49:09.916 --> 49:10.915
He might listen to you.

49:10.916 --> 49:14.582
But you need to show him
that you care about the city.

49:14.583 --> 49:17.833
That everything you do
is for the good of Ba Sing Se.

49:18.791 --> 49:20.708
I could help you with that.

49:21.625 --> 49:23.249
So you're with me?

49:23.250 --> 49:26.166
Of course. Of course I'm with you.

49:26.875 --> 49:28.625
I live to serve Ba Sing Se.

49:29.916 --> 49:34.916
But because our king is so reluctant
to face uncomfortable truths,

49:36.041 --> 49:39.874
I've had to take on so much more
than any cultural minister has.

49:39.875 --> 49:41.625
And sometimes I…

49:43.166 --> 49:44.583
Sorry, I…

49:46.958 --> 49:48.458
I've said too much.

49:49.291 --> 49:51.125
No, Minister.

49:52.250 --> 49:53.166
It's okay.

49:54.958 --> 49:55.916
No.

49:57.041 --> 49:58.583
You're the Avatar.

49:59.833 --> 50:01.833
My burdens are nothing compared to yours.

50:06.333 --> 50:07.708
[Aang] Sometimes,

50:08.500 --> 50:10.583
I feel like there's so much to do.

50:11.208 --> 50:13.957
And I can't even stop to breathe,

50:13.958 --> 50:15.665
because if I do,

50:15.666 --> 50:18.707
what if I miss something

50:18.708 --> 50:20.833
or fail the world

50:21.666 --> 50:22.707
again?

50:22.708 --> 50:24.708
[pensive music playing]

50:27.500 --> 50:28.708
It is

50:29.750 --> 50:30.708
isolating.

50:31.750 --> 50:32.750
Isn't it?

50:35.208 --> 50:36.916
When it gets to be too much…

50:39.416 --> 50:40.416
I talk to Appa.

50:41.416 --> 50:42.375
[Long Feng scoffs]

50:43.208 --> 50:46.374
Does Appa have
any sessions available for me?

50:46.375 --> 50:47.416
[chuckles]

50:50.750 --> 50:51.666
I'll check.

50:52.166 --> 50:53.333
[chuckles]

50:58.333 --> 51:00.208
We will find a solution.

51:00.833 --> 51:01.833
Together.

51:03.458 --> 51:05.250
Okay, Avatar Aang?

51:05.750 --> 51:06.666
Yes.

51:07.958 --> 51:08.958
And

51:10.666 --> 51:11.750
it's just Aang.

51:13.083 --> 51:15.083
Okay. Aang.

51:16.708 --> 51:17.541
[chuckles]

51:27.875 --> 51:29.875
[mysterious music playing]

51:38.875 --> 51:40.124
[girl] Thank you.

51:40.125 --> 51:42.125
[uplifting music playing]

51:48.291 --> 51:52.458
So Long Feng said that if I integrated
into the city and contribute,

51:53.041 --> 51:55.124
the king would be more likely to listen.

51:55.125 --> 51:57.958
Okay. Yeah.
I'm not super sure about that guy.

52:00.291 --> 52:01.166
Oh, hello.

52:01.666 --> 52:02.915
Hey, when did you get back?

52:02.916 --> 52:05.290
I got tired, so I took a carriage.

52:05.291 --> 52:07.291
How did it go with the king?

52:08.166 --> 52:10.415
I didn't quite meet with the king,

52:10.416 --> 52:12.999
but Long Feng said
that he'd do everything in his power

52:13.000 --> 52:14.290
to help arrange a meeting.

52:14.291 --> 52:15.665
It's just gonna take some time.

52:15.666 --> 52:16.541
[Sokka gasps]

52:18.083 --> 52:19.041
We're

52:19.875 --> 52:21.375
all on the ceiling now.

52:21.958 --> 52:24.999
Yeah, he's been like this for hours.

52:25.000 --> 52:29.332
Oh, he drank some… cactus juice?

52:29.333 --> 52:30.250
Oh!

52:31.375 --> 52:33.624
Drink cactus juice. It'll quench ya.

52:33.625 --> 52:36.499
Nothing's quenchier. It's the quenchiest.

52:36.500 --> 52:38.957
No, thank you. It's okay. No, thank you.

52:38.958 --> 52:40.665
[Sokka] Mmm.

52:40.666 --> 52:42.833
My… my… my…

52:43.916 --> 52:46.290
my snoozles.

52:46.291 --> 52:47.624
[Toph] Yeah. Mm-hmm.

52:47.625 --> 52:50.082
Snoozles would be a good idea for you.

52:50.083 --> 52:51.124
For all of us.

52:51.125 --> 52:52.957
Yeah, we're gonna be here for a while,

52:52.958 --> 52:55.832
so we may as well get… comfortable.

52:55.833 --> 52:57.540
Yeah, not you. [chuckles]

52:57.541 --> 53:00.416
We have earthbending training
in the morning.

53:01.000 --> 53:02.041
What time?

53:03.958 --> 53:05.040
I'll wake you up.

53:05.041 --> 53:06.791
- Night.
- Night.

53:07.291 --> 53:08.249
[Sokka] Good night.

53:08.250 --> 53:10.708
It's a giant mushroom.

53:11.250 --> 53:13.333
Maybe it's friendly.

53:14.208 --> 53:15.791
[owl hooting]

53:19.541 --> 53:21.541
[mysterious music playing]

53:34.208 --> 53:35.208
Sai the mechanist.

53:37.250 --> 53:39.250
The king has invited you to Lake Laogai.

53:40.666 --> 53:43.374
Yes, of course.
I'd be happy to go wherever.

53:43.375 --> 53:44.250
Now.

53:45.916 --> 53:46.916
[gulps]

54:12.416 --> 54:13.958
[music swells]

54:15.916 --> 54:17.833
[dramatic, adventurous music playing]

56:26.916 --> 56:27.916
[music ends]
